2. Source code

The corresponding source code for this build is offered in
SOURCE-OFFER.txt, which is installed next to this file. The exact Git
revision used to build the shipped binaries is recorded in the
BUILD-INFO.txt file distributed with the installer.

3. JUCE framework

EarLab is built with the JUCE framework, version 8.0.15, which is
dual-licensed by Raw Material Software Limited under the GNU Affero
General Public License v3 and the JUCE 8 commercial license.

This build is distributed under the AGPLv3 option. Distributing EarLab as
a closed-source or otherwise AGPL-incompatible commercial product
requires a valid JUCE commercial license; until such a license is in
place, EarLab binaries must be distributed under the AGPLv3 together with
their corresponding source code.

JUCE license information:
    https://juce.com/legal/juce-8-licence/

JUCE 8.0.15 source code:
    https://github.com/juce-framework/JUCE/tree/8.0.15

4. Third-party components

See THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt for the full list of bundled third-party
components and their licenses, including the Microsoft Visual C++ 2022
x64 runtime libraries shipped app-local next to the executable.

5. Data and privacy

EarLab stores its user data locally in %APPDATA%\EarLab and does not send
it anywhere. Uninstalling EarLab keeps that folder by default.

6. Internal build status

This installer is an internal engineering build. Before distributing it
to third parties, the JUCE licensing decision above and a CA-signed
release build (instead of the development certificate used here) must be
completed. See the project release checklist.
